{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 48","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the larger base of an isosceles trapezoid equals a diagonal and the smaller base equals the altitude, \nthen the ratio of the smaller base to the larger base is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/daccd55712c652907839e69da6efd2d64affc47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7897dd2f5940ecbbd0857b8c6dd200a7e12355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(1,3)--(4,3)--(5,0)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(4,3)); draw((4,3)--(4,0)); draw((3.8,0)--(3.8,0.2)--(4,0.2)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,3),NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(4,3),NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(5,0),E); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(4,0),S); label(&quot;1&quot;,(2,1.5),NW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of the smaller base of isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the length of the larger base of the trapezoid. The ratio of the smaller base to the larger base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0316e96aae51df608fe04927a8ed7d61fb0a8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a1=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" />. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since the larger base of the isosceles trapezoid equals a diagonal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/92715289dd9f5634bdb56c59c99df2707f09758b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=AD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />. Since the smaller base equals the altitude, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/5992d6926101d392ee7924b889bd4036ab77a26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=CE=a$\" width=\"115\" height=\"12\" />. Since the trapezoid is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c93609dfc247d80cc349d8c76fd0fd52677a001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=\\frac{1-a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb87acf4124ce23941f66d1d4546a358db9039f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 1-\\frac{1-a}{2} = \\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa93f0905263b79480af39c0c867c301e3ec199.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+\\left(\\frac{a+1}{2}\\right)^2=1\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"46\" />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/3118d14c42c205e5e91012a8754b88c8d7869be3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4a^2+(a+1)^2=4\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />\nExpanding the squared binomial and rearranging gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392b6c08f8a85bb3ec23687c8d63b2ef803cbe0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5a^2+2a-3=0\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />\nThis can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee37ab2a0b0a4ce9ba3e2c8c03a3168de25aee41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5a-3)(a+1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />. Since a must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7d188b0fb05385e0697062daf816972d621268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5a+3=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c962478a3a5ae7ee8cc6733ccde6d9c968886b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />. The ratio of the smaller base to the larger base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d58a4119e123308a113c9eb79b29553fd0a7c1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac 35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_47\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 47\">Problem 47</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 49\">Problem 49</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 A